## 4. The Same Idea, Two Products (from Loop Engineering, June 2026)

Both major coding-agent products now ship all five pieces natively — this is presented as a sign the *pattern* has stabilized more than any one tool has won:

| Piece | Job in the loop | Codex app | Claude Code |
|---|---|---|---|
| Automations | Scheduled discovery + triage | Automations tab (project, prompt, cadence, environment) → Triage inbox; `/goal` runs until done | Scheduled tasks, cron, `/loop`, `/goal`, hooks, GitHub Actions |
| Worktrees | Isolate parallel work | Built-in worktree per thread | `git worktree`, `--worktree` flag, `isolation: worktree` on a subagent |
| Skills | Codify project knowledge | Agent Skills (`SKILL.md`), invoked by name or automatically | Agent Skills (`SKILL.md`) |
| Plugins / connectors | Reach real tools | Connectors (MCP) + plugins for distribution | MCP servers + plugins |
| Sub-agents | Ideate and verify | Defined as TOML in `.codex/agents/` | Defined in `.claude/agents/`, plus agent teams |
| State | Track what's done | Markdown, or Linear via connector | Markdown (e.g. `AGENTS.md`, progress files), or Linear via MCP |

